HST Office: a VBA project read from a Word file is written back unchanged.

The owner's test in real Word: a project written by VbaExport gives "Could not open macro storage".
.docm replaced the project on every save, so saving a real Word file in HST, even with no macro
edits, would lose its working macros; .doc did so after edits. The project read from the file is now
copied. When macros were edited, the standard warning says the original code stays and the edits are
not saved. Documents without a project of their own still get what HST writes: that output is not
yet accepted by Word.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba-keep-word-project.py.
